    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "rebuilt? how. everything i built is burned. the people i knew, the life i had... it's not just a setback. it's a total erasure. there's no \"next chapter\" when there's nothing left of the protagonist. i just feel like the world has already moved on from me.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I know it feels like erasure, but that’s the grief talking—it makes everything look final when it’s really just a door slamming shut. You don’t rebuild from the ashes of the old life; you build from the raw material of who you are *now*, even if that feels like nothing. The world may have moved on, but that doesn’t mean you have to—you can start smaller than you think, one breath, one step, one honest moment at a time.",
      "source": "target",
